Package: odrlITR
Type: Package
Title: Orthogonal Double Residual Learning for Treatment Rules
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiaqi", "Tong", email = "jiaqi.tong@yale.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-8922-3386")),
    person("Fan", "Li", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Learns individualized treatment rules with the orthogonal double
    residual loss. First-stage propensity and marginal outcome regressions may
    be estimated by cross-fitted Super Learner or supplied directly by the
    user. The second stage supports direct optimization over linear rules and
    shallow decision trees, as well as hinge- and logistic-loss relaxation
    over kernel and rectified-linear-unit score classes. The implementation
    keeps nuisance estimation, policy optimization, tuning, and prediction in
    separate, auditable components.
